            <ArticleTitle>Floating thrombus in the aortic arch as an origin of simultaneous peripheral emboli.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>762-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1540-8191.2008.00694.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Few cases of a floating thrombus in a normal aorta have been reported without other underlying reasons for the thrombus formation and its systemic embolic complications. We report a case in which a floating thrombus in the proximal aortic arch was detected after echocardiography and computed tomography angiography as an origin of upper extremities and ophthalmic embolism.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
